[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3085080615","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108723#issuecomment-3085080615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108723","id":3085080615,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc634pgn","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-17T18:47:24Z","updated_at":"2025-07-17T18:47:24Z","body":"CC @stuartcarnie \n\nThere's two potential fixes to evaluate here:\n1) We modify the options specified to to the conversion process that it should support the Vulkan Memory Model. The flag exists, but there's no indication of whether DXIL supports whatever this affects.\n2) When using D3D12, we opt for not using this flag instead.\n\nI feel it should be possible to guarantee 1) as long as we have a proper explanation as to why this is necessary.\n\nClay pointed me to the following discussion here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108028#discussion_r2180850546\n\nI can do a PR to fix the issue once we agree on either of these approaches.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3085080615/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3085767484","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108723#issuecomment-3085767484","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108723","id":3085767484,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc637RM8","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-17T23:00:18Z","updated_at":"2025-07-17T23:00:18Z","body":"The pragma removes some of the implicit coherency behaviour of GL450 in favour of Vulkan's explicit requirements. In Metal, without adding the Vulkan memory model, it assumed device coherency, resulting in a declaration (MSL) like:\n\n```metal\nstruct spvDescriptorSetBuffer1\n{\n    constant SceneParams* scene_params [[id(0)]];\n    texture3d<uint, access::read_write, memory_coherence_device> density_only_map [[id(1)]];\n    texture3d<uint, access::read, memory_coherence_device> emissive_only_map [[id(2)]];\n    texture3d<uint, access::read, memory_coherence_device> light_only_map [[id(3)]];\n};\n```\n\nwhich generated more inefficient code, even though all the operations on those maps are atomic.\n\nBy enabling the Vulkan memory model, it drops the `memory_coherence_device` qualifier, improving performance dramatically.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3085767484/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3103047509","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108723#issuecomment-3103047509","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108723","id":3103047509,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc649L9V","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-22T14:34:43Z","updated_at":"2025-07-22T14:35:53Z","body":"> The pragma removes some of the implicit coherency behaviour of GL450 in favour of Vulkan's explicit requirements. In Metal, without adding the Vulkan memory model, it assumed device coherency, resulting in a declaration (MSL) like:\n\nWas vulkanMemoryModel checked for when this was added however? It seems the extension defines that the capability is optional.\n\nhttps://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/latest/man/html/VK_KHR_vulkan_memory_model.html\n> All functionality in this extension is included in core Vulkan 1.2, with the KHR suffix omitted. However, if Vulkan 1.2 is supported and this extension is not, the vulkanMemoryModel capability is optional. The original type, enum, and command names are still available as aliases of the core functionality.\n\nI'm not sure we're actually able to make use of this feature without checking for its support first. It sounds like the proper way to do this would be to introduce a shader variant that bakes depending on whether the device will support it or not.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3103047509/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3109785953","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108723#issuecomment-3109785953","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108723","id":3109785953,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65W5Fh","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","f